  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / Buy for the work</p><h2>Which sales dialler<br>belongs on your shortlist?</h2><p>We judge the usable plan, calling workflow, CRM fit, cost clarity and what needs testing. These are ten relevant options for human callers, grouped around different jobs. Their order is not a ranking.</p></div>
    <div class="dc-shortlist"><div><h3>One caller. Limited list.</h3><p>Start with control over each call, useful notes and callbacks. Single-line power may be enough.</p><p><a href="#close">Close</a> · <a href="#phoneburner">PhoneBurner</a> · <a href="#mojo">Mojo</a></p></div><div><h3>A team doing call blocks.</h3><p>Test parallel calling, answer handling and coaching. Price the minimum seats before the demo.</p><p><a href="#nooks">Nooks</a> · <a href="#orum">Orum</a> · <a href="#kixie">Kixie</a></p></div><div><h3>Keep the existing stack.</h3><p>Check the dialler in your current platform, or add calling that works with your CRM.</p><p><a href="#apollo">Apollo</a> · <a href="#justcall">JustCall</a> · <a href="#aircall">Aircall</a> · <a href="#cloudtalk">CloudTalk</a></p></div></div>
    <p class="lp-scroll-hint">Swipe the table to see pricing and buying checks.</p>
    <div class="lp-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="dc-table-caption"><table class="lp-table dc-table"><caption id="dc-table-caption">10 cold calling diallers: usable plans, prices and limitations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Dialler</th><th scope="col">Workflow and modes</th><th scope="col">Price for the relevant setup</th><th scope="col">Check before buying</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr><th scope="row"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }} ↗</a></th><td>{{ p.fit }}<span class="dc-mode">{{ p.modes }}</span></td><td>{{ p.price }}</td><td>{{ p.catch }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Annual prices are monthly equivalents, not month-to-month offers. Taxes and unlisted extras are excluded. PhoneBurner and Mojo display dollar prices on their US sites without an explicit currency label in the sources reviewed; confirm billing currency. The calculator does not convert currencies. Sources and qualifications appear in each review.</p>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Our blunt take: do not buy speed to hide a list problem.</strong><p>If you call about 300 times a week, first check what slows you down. Research, bad numbers, ringing time and follow-up are different problems. Three hundred attempts can include repeat calls to the same people. Buying ten lines does not create ten times the suitable prospects.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Need the data first? Compare the <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-providers/">10 best B2B lead generation databases</a>, then use our <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">mobile vs company numbers guide</a> to prepare the calling routes.</p>
